WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:08.510
I am thrilled to report to you that the Joe
Biden administration has frozen U.S. weapons

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.530
sales to Saudi Arabia.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:17.700
The Biden administration is freezing to big
arms deals with Saudi Arabia, as well as the

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.690
United Arab Emirates.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:25.590
And these were approved very late in the Trump
administration and they are now on pause.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:33.149
This is related to the sale of some F-35 jets,
as well as attack drones to the UAE and a

00:00:33.149 --> 00:00:39.710
very big supply of various munitions, elements
of munitions to Saudi Arabia.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.450
These are stopped and they are going to be
reviewed.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:48.059
This would be a huge policy shift from the
Trump era and really a big policy shift in

00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:52.199
general for the United States State Department.

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:55.659
And we have been talking about the has it
been I think it's been a decade that I've

00:00:55.659 --> 00:00:58.800
been talking about the perverse relationship
with Saudi.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:06.329
Arabia on this program, the senior U.S. official
who commented on this said that these are

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:10.800
routine administrative actions typical to
any transition.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.149
You just were putting a pause to review pending
arms deals.

00:01:15.149 --> 00:01:20.000
And they sort of are seemingly trying to downplay
the geopolitical significance, but I don't

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.689
think it should be downplayed.

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:25.060
Let's wait and see what they decide if then
they say in a month.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.140
Oh, yeah, we're going to just go through with
it.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:30.189
Well, then maybe really this is no big deal.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:36.369
But so far, this appears to be a significant
a significant decision that's being made.

00:01:36.369 --> 00:01:39.850
I like what I see now.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:45.579
If we think about engagement with the progressive
base of the Democratic Party, as well as more

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:50.420
left leaning independents, this is a good
step by the Biden administration.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:55.630
Of course, it remains to be seen what ultimately
happens with these paused deals.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:58.450
But so far, there is a lot to be optimistic
about.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:02.810
And very importantly, this reminds us both
sides aren't the same.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:09.650
Trump spent his administration bragging about
arms deals with Saudi Arabia.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:15.659
When asked about stopping the deals over the
murder of Jamal Khashoggi, he said, well,

00:02:15.659 --> 00:02:16.930
there's a lot of jobs out there.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:17.940
Remember this?

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:26.650
Jamal Khashoggi, the journalist, the Saudi
journalist, was he murdered by the Saudis?

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.470
And did the prince give the order to kill
him?

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.650
Well, nobody knows yet, but we'll probably
be able to find out.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.350
It's being investigated.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.680
It's being looked at very, very strongly.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:40.450
And we would be very upset and angry if that
were the case as of this moment.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.930
They deny it and then deny it vehemently.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:44.989
Could it be them?

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:45.989
Yes.

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:51.370
Jared, your son in law's got on the phone
and asked the prince, did he what?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.370
Did he deny it?

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:53.370
Did they deny it?

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.459
They denied every way you can imagine in the
not too distant future.

00:02:56.459 --> 00:02:58.090
I think we'll know an answer.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.150
What are your options?

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.930
Let's say they did.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.319
What are your options?

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:08.939
Would you consider imposing sanctions as a
bipartisan group of senators have proposed?

00:03:08.939 --> 00:03:10.010
What depends on what the sanctions.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.989
I'll give you an example.

00:03:11.989 --> 00:03:14.700
They are ordering military equipment.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.580
Everybody in the world wanted that order.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:17.950
Russia wanted it.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.260
China wanted it.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.610
We wanted it.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:21.610
We got it.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:22.630
So would you cut that off?

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:28.459
Well, I tell you what I don't want to do Boeing,
Lockheed, Raytheon, all these.

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:30.900
I don't want to hurt jobs.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.950
Here's another one where Donald Trump was
asked about the same thing.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:40.049
Be in favor of stopping a country from spending
one hundred and ten billion dollars, which

00:03:40.049 --> 00:03:45.360
is an all time record, and letting Russia
have that money and letting China have that

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.060
money, because all they're going to do is
say, that's OK, we don't have to buy it from

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.180
Boeing.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:55.840
We don't have to buy it from Lockheed, we
don't have to buy it from Raytheon.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.010
And all these great companies will buy it
from Russia, will buy it from China.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.879
So what good does that do us?

00:04:01.879 --> 00:04:03.890
There are other things we can do now.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:04.890
Donald Trump is not wrong.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:11.670
I mean, Trump is right that there are U.S.
there are jobs in the United States connected

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.049
to selling weapons to Saudi Arabia.

00:04:14.049 --> 00:04:15.409
That's true.

00:04:15.409 --> 00:04:18.430
What makes the freeze all the more notable?

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:25.290
And if they stick to it and cancel the deals,
all the more brave is that there are jobs

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:30.070
connected to this and there will be people
who say anything that creates jobs must be

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:36.310
done, no matter how unethical or immoral or
counter to our stated values as a country.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:41.330
If Joe Biden sticks with not going through
with these sales, there will be some jobs

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:42.330
on the line.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:43.410
That's true.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:48.250
And it will make what is a morally correct
decision all the more significant.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:53.870
I didn't expect to see this yesterday and
I am quite pleased we will follow it to see

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.300
where it ends up.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.440
Let me know your thoughts.

